ing d2-d4 comfortably\n- Follows classical opening principles\n\nReason: e7-e5 is the strongest move as it immediately stakes a claim in the center, opens development lines for my pieces, and puts pressure on White's position. This classical central pawn advance is particularly effective when White has made an early knight development to c3, as it prevents White from easily establishing a strong pawn center.\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5"}
