g outpost. It controls critical central squares, attacks White's weak points around the king (e2), and cannot be easily displaced by pawns. This move maintains the initiative while improving piece coordination, and it's much more solid than premature queen or pawn advances.\n\nAnswer: N: c6-d4"}
