y knight on an excellent square attacking key central squares\n- White cannot easily challenge this knight\n\nReason: N: d4-f3+ delivers check, forcing White's king to move and permanently losing castling rights. This is a critical tactical blow that gains tempo while improving my knight's position. The disruption to White's king safety is significant and gives me a clear advantage in the position.\n\nAnswer: N: d4-f3"}
