 where it has more piece protection.\n\nReason: Moving K: e8-d8 keeps my king on the back rank where it's better protected by my other pieces (rooks on a8 and h8, bishops on c8 and f8). This move gets the king out of check while maintaining defensive solidity. Moving forward to e7 or toward d7 would expose the king more dangerously in the center of the board.\n\nAnswer: K: e8-d8"}
