ision:**\nThe rook move R: h8-g8 is most logical because:\n- It activates my most powerful remaining piece\n- It prepares potential back-rank pressure\n- It keeps my king flexible for future moves\n- It's a developing move that improves my position without creating weaknesses\n\nEvaluation: I'm in a difficult position being down material (no queen vs opponent's queen). My priority should be rapid piece development and creating whatever counterplay possible. The rook on h8 is my most powerful piece and needs to enter the game.\n\nReason: Activating the rook with h8-g8 develops my strongest piece, maintains flexibility for my king, and prepares to contest important files. This is more constructive than passive bishop development or premature pawn advances.\n\nAnswer: R: h8-g8"}
